  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Business Development Initiatives - IDEE Youth</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To support the Government of Niger (GoN) in addressing the challenges related to youth employment and the socio-economic conditions inciting young people to irregular migration exposing them to risks of exploitation and abuse, IOM in Niger has been implementing the IDEE - Initiatives for Enterprise Development project since 2017. This third phase of the IDEE project aims to promote the economic inclusion of young people (men and women) through entrepreneurship and the enhancement of skills adapted to the country&apos;s production and labor market needs. The project is part of the ongoing drive to increase economic opportunities for young people, by supporting entrepreneurial initiatives and including other vulnerable groups, more specifically women, people with disabilities and returning migrants. The project will be implemented in four target regions: Tahoua, Zinder, Niamey, and Agadez, which are mainly areas of departure (Zinder, Tahoua) and arrival or transit of migrants (Niamey and Agadez). The project will focus on vocational training and Niger&apos;s entrepreneurial fabric, with a view to supporting the most vulnerable young people and women in setting up micro-enterprises and expanding production activities. Priority will be given to women&apos;s entrepreneurial initiatives and to people living with disabilities. The project will support groups of women producers and micro-enterprises applying virtuous and innovative techniques (hiring young apprentices, recycling, renewable energies).</narrative>
  </description>
